---
import ProductPricing from '../../components/ProductPricing.astro';
import DemoLink from '../../components/DemoLink.astro';
import DemoSwitch from '../../components/DemoSwitch.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
    title="Directory Services Portal"
    description="Directory Services Portal is a web front end for LDAP directories with custom schemas: administrators build forms for any object class, publish them as scoped directories, and grant read and write access to users and groups. From ENS Solutions."
>
<section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
        <a class="backlink" href="/">&larr; All products</a>
        <div class="title-row">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--inline">Directory Services Portal &middot; Web front end for LDAP</p>
            <span class="badge badge--live">Available</span>
        </div>
        <h1>Your directory&rsquo;s own schema, as forms people can use.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
            Directory Services Portal puts a web front end on LDAP directories, including those with
            custom, non-standard schemas. Administrators build forms for any object class, publish them
            as directories scoped to one part of the tree, and decide who can read or edit each one.
            Every user gets a profile page showing where they appear and what they can update
            themselves &mdash; without anyone needing an LDAP browser.
        </p>

        <div class="btn-row">
            <DemoSwitch product="directory-portal">
                <Fragment slot="demo">
                    <DemoLink product="directory-portal" />
                    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#how-heading">See how it works</a>
                    <span class="btn-note">Opens the Directory Services Portal demo environment in a new tab.</span>
                </Fragment>
                <Fragment slot="nodemo">
                    <span class="btn btn--disabled" aria-disabled="true">Demo unavailable</span>
                    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#how-heading">See how it works</a>
                    <span class="btn-note">No demo URL is configured for this deployment.</span>
                </Fragment>
            </DemoSwitch>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="how-heading">How it works</h2>
        <p class="lede">Administrators set it up once, and people use it from any browser.</p>
        <ol class="flow-steps">
            <li>
                <strong>Load the schema.</strong> Read it straight from the directory, including
                non-standard object classes and attributes, or import OpenLDAP schema files and
                <span class="mono">cn=config</span> LDIF. Add display names and descriptions, or define
                elements the server does not publish.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Build a form.</strong> Pick the object classes and the editor suggests their
                attributes, then warns about schema problems before they reach the directory. Fields can
                be text, text areas or drop-downs, including drop-downs filled from a directory search.
                For example, choose a manager by name and store their DN.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Publish it as a directory.</strong> Link the form to a base DN, a scope and an
                optional filter. The portal only reads or writes entries inside that part of the tree.
                Choose read/write, or a read-only &ldquo;white pages&rdquo; that nobody can write through,
                administrators included.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Grant access.</strong> Give users or directory groups view, or view-and-edit, access to
                each directory. A matrix shows every grant at a glance.
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="screens-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="screens-heading">See it in use</h2>
        <p class="lede">Screenshots of Directory Services Portal running against a demo directory with sample people and data. Select one to see it full size.</p>
        <div class="shot-grid">
            <figure class="shot shot--wide">
                <a href="/assets/img/screens/directory-portal-staff.jpg" class="shot-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                    <picture>
                        <source media="(max-width: 640px)" srcset="/assets/img/screens/directory-portal-staff-mobile.jpg" width="620" height="560">
                        <img src="/assets/img/screens/directory-portal-staff.jpg" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                             alt="Directory Services Portal staff directory: a searchable table of employees with job title, department, e-mail and phone, and a New employee button.">
                    </picture>
                    <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens full size in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
                <figcaption><strong>A directory.</strong> A published form becomes a searchable, sortable list that people with access can edit.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="shot">
                <a href="/assets/img/screens/directory-portal-form-editor.jpg" class="shot-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                    <picture>
                        <source media="(max-width: 640px)" srcset="/assets/img/screens/directory-portal-form-editor-mobile.jpg" width="640" height="780">
                        <img src="/assets/img/screens/directory-portal-form-editor.jpg" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                             alt="Directory Services Portal form editor for an Employee form built on inetOrgPerson plus a custom acmePerson class, listing fields marked required, self-service, multi-valued or read only.">
                    </picture>
                    <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens full size in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
                <figcaption><strong>Form editor.</strong> Build a form from any object classes, including custom schema, and mark each field required, self-service or read only.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="shot">
                <a href="/assets/img/screens/directory-portal-audit.jpg" class="shot-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                    <picture>
                        <source media="(max-width: 640px)" srcset="/assets/img/screens/directory-portal-audit-mobile.jpg" width="680" height="690">
                        <img src="/assets/img/screens/directory-portal-audit.jpg" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                             alt="Directory Services Portal audit log: sign-ins, entry updates and a denied edit, with one update expanded to show who made it, from where, and the job title before and after.">
                    </picture>
                    <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens full size in a new tab)</span>
                </a>
                <figcaption><strong>Audit log.</strong> Every change and sign-in, with who made it and what changed, including edits the portal refused.</figcaption>
            </figure>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="users-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="users-heading">For the people in the directory</h2>
        <div class="card-grid card-grid--pairs">
            <article class="card">
                <p class="card-kicker">Directories</p>
                <h3>Search, browse and edit</h3>
                <p>
                    Each directory is a searchable, sortable list. Entries can be viewed, created, edited
                    and deleted according to the user&rsquo;s access. Only changed values are written,
                    and changing the naming attribute renames the entry.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <p class="card-kicker">My profile</p>
                <h3>Everywhere you appear, in one place</h3>
                <p>
                    Each user sees every directory that lists them and can update the fields marked
                    self-service, such as a phone number, without raising a ticket.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <p class="card-kicker">Validation</p>
                <h3>Checked twice before it reaches the directory</h3>
                <p>
                    Required fields, single-value rules, allowed options, formats (email, phone, URL,
                    number, DN), patterns and length limits are checked in the browser and again on the
                    server.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <p class="card-kicker">Sign-in</p>
                <h3>Directory password or smart card</h3>
                <p>
                    Users sign in with their own directory password, or with a client certificate such
                    as a CAC or PIV card. Each certificate is mapped to exactly one directory user. The
                    portal can also be set to accept certificates only.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="security-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="security-heading">Security</h2>
        <div class="feature-grid">
            <div class="feature">
                <h3>Certificates checked before mapping</h3>
                <p>
                    Validity dates, client-authentication key usage and, optionally, the chain to your
                    CAs and revocation (OCSP or CRL). Optionally, the certificate must also be the one
                    published on the user&rsquo;s entry.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature">
                <h3>Namespaces enforced on the server</h3>
                <p>
                    Every DN is parsed and checked against the directory&rsquo;s base, scope and filter,
                    and writes are limited to the form&rsquo;s writable fields. User input in filters is
                    always escaped.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature">
                <h3>Hardened sessions</h3>
                <p>
                    HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict session cookies, a new session ID at sign-in, CSRF
                    protection on every change, login throttling, and password attributes that
                    are never sent to the browser.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="tech-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="tech-heading">What you need to run it</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll">
            <table>
                <caption class="visually-hidden">Directory Services Portal technical summary</caption>
                <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Component</th>
                    <th scope="col">Detail</th>
                </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">API</th>
                    <td>Spring Boot 4 on Java 21, using the UnboundID LDAP SDK over a pooled service-account connection</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Web client</th>
                    <td>A static React build served by nginx, which forwards <span class="mono">/api</span> to the API so the browser sees a single origin</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Directory</th>
                    <td>Any LDAP / LDAPS server, with StartTLS supported. The service account needs read access to the schema and the exposed parts of the tree, and write access wherever users edit</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Storage</th>
                    <td>No database. Forms, directories, grants and custom schema are kept in a single JSON configuration file</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Authentication</th>
                    <td>Password sign-in verified by an LDAP bind; optional mutual TLS, ended at the web proxy or at the API</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row">Deployment</th>
                    <td>Separate containers for the web client and the API, plus a Docker Compose stack with a demo OpenLDAP server</td>
                </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div class="callout">
            <p>
                Want to see Directory Services Portal against your own schema?
                <a href="/contact.html?product=directory-portal">Get in touch</a> or email
                <a href="mailto:info@ens-solutions.com">info@ens-solutions.com</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<ProductPricing product="directory-portal">
    <p class="muted">
        Custom schema mappings and form work beyond what your administrators build themselves are billed as
        time and materials. <a href="/pricing.html#services-heading">See services</a>.
    </p>
</ProductPricing>
</BaseLayout>
